WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.927
Security telemetry helps teams understand who accessed the system, which service acted,

00:00:04.927 --> 00:00:08.949
what policy decision occurred, and what sensitive resource was involved.

00:00:08.949 --> 00:00:10.155
In AI platforms,

00:00:10.155 --> 00:00:14.982
that visibility may need to cover ordinary application access plus model gateways,

00:00:14.982 --> 00:00:18.602
retrieval systems, tool-use workflows, human approval steps, administrative changes,

00:00:18.602 --> 00:00:19.808
and service identities.

00:00:19.808 --> 00:00:23.026
Useful defensive signals include authentication results, authorization decisions,

00:00:23.026 --> 00:00:26.646
denied actions, service identity use, administrative changes, secret access,

00:00:26.646 --> 00:00:29.461
policy evaluation outcomes, and unusual access patterns.

00:00:29.461 --> 00:00:34.288
These signals help operators investigate whether a request followed the intended path

00:00:34.288 --> 00:00:37.104
and whether controls behaved consistently across clusters,

00:00:37.104 --> 00:00:38.712
environments, and data sources.

00:00:38.712 --> 00:00:41.528
AI-specific workflows can make access questions subtle.

00:00:41.528 --> 00:00:46.354
A user may be allowed to call an assistant but not allowed

00:00:46.354 --> 00:00:49.572
to retrieve every document the assistant can search.

00:00:49.572 --> 00:00:54.801
A service may be allowed to use one model route but not another.

00:00:54.801 --> 00:01:00.432
A tool invocation may require approval, a policy check, or a narrower runtime identity.

00:01:00.432 --> 00:01:04.052
Telemetry should show the decision without exposing protected content.

00:01:04.052 --> 00:01:05.661
Privacy-aware logging is essential.

00:01:05.661 --> 00:01:10.889
Logs and audit records should avoid secrets, credentials, raw sensitive prompts, personal data,

00:01:10.889 --> 00:01:12.498
and protected source material.

00:01:12.498 --> 00:01:14.509
The goal is structured, searchable,

00:01:14.509 --> 00:01:17.727
time-aware evidence connected to request or workload context.

00:01:17.727 --> 00:01:21.749
Security telemetry is not about collecting the most sensitive information.

00:01:21.749 --> 00:01:24.565
It is about defensive visibility, accountable operations,

00:01:24.565 --> 00:01:27.380
and faster investigation with appropriate data minimization.
